"hadiths[42]{hadithnumber,text}:"
999,"Narrated `Abdullah bin `Umar:\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) concluded a contract with the people of Khaibar to utilize the land on the condition that \nhalf the products of fruits or vegetation would be their share. The Prophet (ﷺ) used to give his wives one \nhundred Wasqs each, eighty Wasqs of dates and twenty Wasqs of barley. (When `Umar became the \nCaliph) he gave the wives of the Prophet (ﷺ) the option of either having the land and water as their shares, \nor carrying on the previous practice. Some of them chose the land and some chose the Wasqs, and \n`Aisha chose the land."""
1000,"`Umar expelled the Jews and the Christians from Hijaz. When Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) had conquered Khaibar, he wanted to expel the Jews from it as its land became the property of Allah, His Apostle, and the Muslims. Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) intended to expel the Jews but they requested him to let them stay there on the condition that they would do the labor and get half of the fruits. Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) told them, We will let you stay on thus condition"""
1001,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, There is none amongst the Muslims who plants a tree or sows seeds ""1002"",It has been narrated on the authority of Abu Sa'id Khudri that a man came to the Prophet (may peace he upon him) and said:Who is the best of men? He replied: A man who fights in the way of Allah spending his wealth and staking his life. The man then asked: Who is next to him (in excellence)? He said: Next to him is a believer who lives in a mountain gorge worshipping hid Lord and sparing men from his mischief"""
1002,"[AI-translation] Hadith of Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, forbade the sale of fruits until they ripen. It was said to him: ""And what is meant by ripening?"" He said: ""Until they turn red."" He said: ""What do you think, if Allah withholds the fruit, by what right does one of you take his brother's wealth?""
1003"""
1003,"Narrated 'Aishah: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) heard the voice of two disputants at the door, their voices being raised, and one of them was asking the other to reduce (something owed to him) and to be lenient with him regarding some matter, while the other was saying: ""By Allah, I will not do it."" So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came out to them and said: ""Where is the one who swears by Allah that he will not do a good deed?"" The man said: ""I am he, O Messenger of Allah, and he may have whichever of the two he prefers."""
1004,"Narrated `Abdullah bin Ka`b bin Malik:\n\nKa`b demanded his debt back from Ibn Abi Hadrad in the Mosque and their voices grew louder till \nAllah's Messenger (ﷺ) heard them while he was in his house. He came out to them raising the curtain of his \nroom and addressed Ka`b, \O Ka`b!\"" Ka`b replied"""
1005,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, ""If a man finds his very things with a bankrupt, he has more right to take them back than anyone else."""""""
1006,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Before your time the angels received the soul of a man and asked him, 'Did you do any good deeds (in your life)?' He replied, 'I used to order my employees to grant time to the rich person to pay his debts at his convenience.' So Allah said to the angels; ""Excuse him."" Rabi said that (the dead man said), 'I used to be easy to the rich and grant time to the poor.' Or, in another narration, 'grant time to the well-off and forgive the needy,' or, 'accept from the well-off and forgive the needy.' ""1007"",Anas reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:If the son of Adam were to possess two valleys of riches. he would long for the third one. And the stomach of the son of Adam is not filled but with dust. And Allah returns to him who repents"""
1007,"[AI-translation] Hadith of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: A merchant used to give credit to people. When he saw one in distress, he would say to his young men: ""Forgive him, perhaps Allah will forgive us."" So Allah forgave him.""
1008"""
1008,"Narrated Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Procrastination (delay) in payment by a wealthy person is injustice (oppression). So if the debt of any one of you is transferred from his debtor to a rich person, he should agree."""
1009,"A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him"""
1010,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, It is not lawful for a lady to fast (Nawafil) without the permission of her husband when he is at home; and she should not allow anyone to enter his house except with his permission; and if she spends of his wealth (on charitable purposes) without being ordered by him"""
1011,"`Umar asked the people, Who remembers the narration of the Prophet (ﷺ) about the affliction?"" Hudhaifa said"""
1012,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, If someone keeps a dog neither for guarding livestock"""
1013,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, Whoever keeps a dog"""
1014,"A'isha (Allah be pleased with her), wife of Allah's Apostle (ﷺ), heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:If your people, had not been recent converts to Islam, I would have spent the treasure of the Ka'ba in the way of Allah and would have constructed its door just on the level of the ground and would have encompassed in it the space of Hijr"""
1015,"that he was asked about the wages of the one who cups others. He said, 'Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) was cupped by `Abd Taiba, to whom he gave two Sa of food and interceded for him with his masters who consequently reduced what they used to charge him daily. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) s said, ""The best medicines you may treat yourselves with are cupping and sea incense.' He added, ""You should not torture your children by treating tonsillitis by pressing the tonsils or the palate with the finger, but use incense."""""""
1016,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, ""Amongst the trees, there is a tree, the leaves of which do not fall and is like a Muslim. Tell me the name of that tree."" Everybody started thinking about the trees of the desert areas. And I thought of the date-palm tree but felt shy to answer the others then asked, ""What is that tree, O Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) ?"" He replied, ""It is the date-palm tree."""""""
1017,"Narrated `Aisha:\n\nWhen the verses of Surat \Al-Baqara\""' about the usury Riba were revealed"""
1018,"That he heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) describing the period of pause of the Divine Inspiration, and in his description he said, ""While I was walking I heard a voice from the sky. I looked up towards the sky, and behold! I saw the same Angel who came to me in the Cave of Hira', sitting on a chair between the sky and the earth. I was so terrified by him that I fell down on the ground. Then I went to my wife and said, 'Wrap me in garments! Wrap me in garments!' They wrapped me, and then Allah revealed: ""O you, (Muhammad) wrapped-up! Arise and warn...and desert the idols."" (74.1-5) Abu Salama said....Rujz means idols."" After that, the Divine Inspiration started coming more frequently and regularly."""
1019,"I proceeded till I entered upon `Umar (and while I was sitting there), his gate-keeper Yarfa came to him and said,  `Uthman"""
1020,"A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him ""1021"",When the mountain of Uhud came in the sight of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) he said. This is a mountain that loves us and is loved by us. O Allah! Abraham made Mecca a sanctuary ""1022"",This hadith has been narrated on the authority of Shu'ba through a different chain of transmitters ""1023"",Abd al-Rabman b. Abia Bakra reported on the authority of his father that Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) forbade the sale of gold for gold"""
1021,"[AI-translation] Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Do not sell gold for gold except like for like, and do not give preference to some of it over some. Do not sell silver for silver except like for like, and do not give preference to some of it over some. And do not sell from it the absent for the present.""
1022"""
1022,"Narrated Abu Al-Minhal: I asked Al-Bara' bin 'Azib and Zaid bin Arqam about As-Sarf (money exchange), and each of them would say, ""This one is better than me."" But both of them said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade selling gold for silver on credit."
1023,"Narrated Abu Bakrah (رضي الله عنه): The Prophet (ﷺ) forbade the exchange of silver for silver, and gold for gold, unless it was equal for equal, and he commanded us to buy gold with silver however we wished, and to buy silver with gold however we wished."
1024,"Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri and Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) appointed a man over Khaibar, and he brought him some Janib (superior quality) dates. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Are all the dates of Khaibar like this?"" He said: ""No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah! We take a Sa' of these for two Sa's, and two Sa's for three."" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Do not do that. Sell the mixed dates for money (Dirhams), and then buy Janib with the money."""
1025,"Once Bilal brought Barni (i.e. a kind of dates) to the Prophet (ﷺ) and the Prophet (ﷺ) asked him, From where have you brought these?"" Bilal replied"""
1026,"We used to be given mixed dates (from the booty) and used to sell (barter) two Sas of those dates) for one Sa (of good dates). The Prophet (ﷺ) said (to us), No (bartering of) two Sas for one Sa nor two Dirhams for one Dirham is permissible"""""""
1027,"I heard Ab Sa'id Al-Khudri r:e d u saying, The selling of a Dind fa Dindr"""
1028,"I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, Who ever is pleased that he be granted more wealth and that his lease of life be pro longed"""
1029,"Narrated Jabir:\n\nWhile I was riding a (slow) and tired camel, the Prophet (ﷺ) passed by and beat it and prayed for Allah's \nBlessings for it. The camel became so fast as it had never been before. The Prophet (ﷺ) then said, \Sell it \nto me for one Uqiyya (of gold).\"" I said"""
1030,"Jabir b. Abdullah (Allah be pleased with them) reported:Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) visited the orchard of Umm Ma'sud and said: Umm Ma'bad. he who has planted this tree, is he a Muslim or a non-Muslim? She said: Of course, he is a Muslim, whereupon he (the Holy Prophet) said: No Muslim who plants (trees) and from their fruits the human beings or the beasts or birds eat, but that would be taken as an act of charity on the Day of Resurrection ""1031"",A hadith like this has been narrated on the authority of Juraij with the same chain of transmitters"""
1031,"[AI-translation] Hadith of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, bought from me a camel for two Waqiyahs and a dirham or two dirhams. When he arrived at Sirar, he ordered a cow to be slaughtered, and they ate from it. When he arrived in Al-Madinah, he ordered me to go to the mosque and pray two rak'ahs, and he weighed out for me the price of the camel.""
1032"""
1032,"Narrated Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him): A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) demanding payment of a debt, and he spoke harshly. The Companions intended to deal with him (harshly), but the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Leave him, for the one who has a right has a right to speak."" Then he said: ""Give him a camel of the same age as his."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah, we can only find one better than his."" He said: ""Give it to him, for the best among you is he who discharges his debt in the best manner."""
1033,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Faith (Belief) consists of more than sixty branches (i.e. parts). And Haya (This term ""Haya"" covers a large number of concepts which are to be taken together; amongst them are self respect, modesty, bashfulness, and scruple, etc.) is a part of faith."""""""
1034,"The Prophet (ﷺ) came to Medina and the people used to pay in advance the price of dates to be delivered within two or three years. He said (to them), Whoever pays in advance the price of a thing to be delivered later should pay it for a specified measure at specified weight for a specified period."""""""""
1035,"I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, Nothing is left of the prophetism except Al-Mubashshirat."" They asked"""
1036,"Narrated Jabir bin `Abdullah:\n\nAllah's Messenger (ﷺ) gave a verdict regarding Shuf'a in every undivided joint thing (property). But if the \nlimits are defined (or demarcated) or the ways and streets are fixed, then there is no pre-emption."""
1037,"A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him"""
1038,"Hudhaifa b. Usaid reported:Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) was in an apartment and we were beneath that, that he peeped in and said to us: What are you discussing about? We said: (We are discussing about the Last) Hour. Thereupon he said: The Last Hour would not come until the ten signs appear: land-sliding in the east, and land-sliding in the west, and land-sliding in the peninsula of Arabia, the smoke, the Dajjal, the beast of the earth, Gog and Magog, the rising of the sun from the west and the fire which would emit from the lower part of 'Adan. Shu'ba said that 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Rufai' reported on the authority of Abu Tufail who reported on the authority of Abu Sariha a hadith like this that Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) did not make a mention of (the tenth sign) but he said that out of the ten one was the descent of Jesus, son of Mary (peace be upon him), and in another version it is the blowing of the violent gale which would drive the people to the ocean"""
1039,"That there was a dispute between him and some people (about a piece of land). When he told `Aisha about it, she said, ""O Abu Salama! Avoid taking the land unjustly, for the Prophet (ﷺ) said, 'Whoever usurps even one span of the land of somebody, his neck will be encircled with it down the seven earths."""" ""1040"",Abu Huraira reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:Whenever you sight the new moon (of the month of Ramadan) observe fast. and when you sight it (the new moon of Shawwal) break it"""
1040,"[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Prophet gave judgment, when they disputed over a road, that it should be seven cubits."""
